Offline engine compatibility fixtures
engines/wega/tests/fixtures contains bundled jQuery 3.7.1, React/ReactDOM 18.3.1,
Vue 3.5.22, Preact 10.27.2, Angular 20.3.0 and RxJS 7.8.2 (MIT).
Their license notices and package versions are included beside the fixtures.

Wega's V8 script host
The independent Wega engine embeds V8 through deno_core. V8 is BSD-3-Clause;
rusty_v8, deno_core, deno_ops and serde_v8 are MIT. Their notices are included in
the engine's generated WEGA-ENGINE-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.html distribution artifact.

Deno Web APIs (MIT)
The engine uses deno_webidl, deno_web, deno_fetch, deno_net, deno_tls,
deno_webstorage, deno_websocket and deno_crypto. Wega's runtime source adapter
adds the HTML Document-to-Window event parent rule to Deno's EventTarget. The
event/fetch dependency source files remain unmodified; the adapter is in
engines/wega/src/extension_adapter.rs and retains the original MIT source headers. Runtime
telemetry collection/export is disabled.

Web Platform Tests
The engine's pinned DOM conformance tests and harness are from
https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt under BSD-3-Clause. The revision,
checksums and original license are included in engines/wega/tests/fixtures/wpt/.

Wega cookie storage uses cookie_store (MIT/Apache-2.0) and publicsuffix
(MIT/Apache-2.0). engines/network/src/public_suffix_list.dat is the MPL-2.0
Public Suffix List snapshot bundled in publicsuffix 2.3.0; its header is retained.
Deno fetch's pinned source is adapted at extension load to attach browser cookies
and ingest Set-Cookie on every redirect hop. Original MIT sources are unchanged.

Deno core extension embedding
Modified by Wega contributors, 2026: engines/vendor/deno/patches/
embed-extension-sources.patch embeds eager and lazy extension JavaScript into
non-snapshot workers. The original MIT license is retained.

The P4-P6 engine uses anyrender_skia 0.12.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and Skia
m153-0.101.2 (BSD-3-Clause). The static Skia notice and original Blitz/anyrender
license texts are shipped in WEGA-ENGINE-NATIVE-LICENSES. Checksummed published
sources and the exact local Blitz, Stylo, Skia adapter and Deno patches are listed
in engines/vendor/sources.json and engines/vendor/README.md.
The pinned CSS WPT subset is licensed under the original WPT license included in
engines/wega/tests/fixtures/css-wpt/LICENSE.md; upstream assertions are unchanged.
